# Store roots created under a crate directory when a test or a `swarmctl` run
# takes a cwd-relative `data/...` default.
#
# These are ENUMERATED on purpose. The blanket `crates/*/data/` that replaced
# the previous list also swallowed every store root that has NEVER leaked, and
# `git rm --cached` had already removed the tracked copies -- so a fresh leak at
# e.g. `crates/swarm-runtime/data/evolution-population/` stopped showing up as
# `?? crates/swarm-runtime/data/` and the CI drift gate went quiet. The
# instruction that produced 2b25bc8 was to untrack, not to ignore; doing both is
# what blinds the gate. Only the roots that 2b25bc8 actually untracked are
# listed, so any NEW leak path stays visible to `git status --porcelain`.
#
# This list is a convenience, not the gate. The binding check is the
# `find crates -maxdepth 2 -name data -type d` assertion in
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, which is immune to .gitignore and also catches
# the EMPTY directories `git status` never reports.
crates/*/data/approval-ledgers/
crates/*/data/approval-receipt-packs/
crates/*/data/approval-sets/
crates/*/data/approval-verdicts/
crates/*/data/evolution-assurance-cases/
crates/*/data/incidents/
crates/*/data/investigations/
crates/*/data/replay/
crates/*/dead-letter.jsonl
.claude/
data/replay-runs/
data/experiments/
data/verifications/
data/shadows/
data/promotion-reviews/
data/canaries/
data/promotions/
data/strategy-memory/
data/strategy-scorecards/
data/evolution-proofs/
data/evolution-queue/
data/evolution-handoffs/
data/evolution-pressures/
data/evolution-drafts/
data/evolution-draft-promotions/
data/evolution-materializations/
data/evolution-validation-bundles/
data/evolution-reconciliations/
data/evolution-mutations/
data/evolution-mutation-materialization-batches/
data/evolution-mutation-validation-batches/
data/evolution-rankings/
data/evolution-selections/
data/evolution-selection-bridges/
data/evolution-portfolios/
data/evolution-governance-review-packets/
data/evolution-packet-sets/
data/evolution-portfolio-history/
# correlation.incident_store for rulesets-dev/perch-dev.yaml (local_files, cwd-relative).
data/incidents/
# Runtime state the daemon writes beside a config that is not under rulesets/
# (rulesets-dev/perch-dev.yaml): the identity registry and the partition
# governance state. Agent keys under it are covered by **/data/agent-keys/.
rulesets-dev/data/agent-identity/
rulesets-dev/governance-partition-state.json

# Agent signing keys. rulesets/data/agent-keys/sphinx-primary.ed25519 was committed
# from 69814a4 until the repo went public, so FileAgentKeyStore::load_or_create
# loaded one shared, world-readable identity instead of minting a per-deployment
# key. Never commit key material; `tools/check-no-committed-keys.sh` enforces this.
**/data/agent-keys/
*.ed25519
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# Subagent-driven-development scratch workspace (ledgers, briefs, review packages).
# The skill assumes this is git-ignored; it was not, so an SDD run left an empty
# directory that the CI drift gate counts as residue.
.superpowers/

# The Perch plan set (docs/plans/ambush-ui/build/) was silently excluded by the
# Python `build/` pattern above; re-include it explicitly.
!docs/plans/ambush-ui/build/

# workspace/ (the Ambush workspace, merged 2026-09-02) carries tracked files that
# the engine's generic patterns above would shadow for future adds. Re-include
# them explicitly; the workspace has its own .gitignore for everything else.
!workspace/**/build/
!workspace/**/build/**
!workspace/.claude/
!workspace/.vscode/
!workspace/crates/ambush-push-gateway/tests/fixtures/*.pem
